##exploring tuples, tuples are just like list but you cant change the content after you create them. its good for creating content that 
you dont want anyone to have access to change anything.
#create tuple
coordinates = (3, 4)
print(coordinates)

#tuple can contain items of different types, for example the following.
person = ("Alice", 25, "Engineer")
name, age, occupation = person  # Tuple unpacking, use for assign multiple variables at one go
#refer to screenshot pss45 in readme.md for result
print(f"{name} is {age} years old and works as an {occupation}.")

#tuple is often used for returning mutiple values from a function
